Built-in classes instantiated with call parentheses inside a class method
(diag.class_instantiation_curly): Email() and SSLRegex(...) flag, with the
curly form in the message. Near misses: Email{} and SSLDataset{} (correct
form) and oSvc:Email("to") (a member call that shares the class name,
issue #32).
-- input.ssl --
:CLASS Notifier;
:DECLARE oSvc;

:PROCEDURE Send;
	:PARAMETERS sTo;
	:DECLARE oMail, oGood, oData, oPattern, vSent;
	oMail := Email();
	oPattern := SSLRegex("^[a-z]+$");
	oGood := Email{};
	oData := SSLDataset{};
	vSent := Me:oSvc:Email(sTo);
	:RETURN vSent;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:CLASS Notifier;
:DECLARE oSvc;

:PROCEDURE Send;
	:PARAMETERS sTo;
	:DECLARE oMail, oGood, oData, oPattern, vSent;

	oMail := Email();
	oPattern := SSLRegex("^[a-z]+$");
	oGood := Email{};
	oData := SSLDataset{};
	vSent := Me:oSvc:Email(sTo);

	:RETURN vSent;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
7:11-7:16 error class_instantiation_curly: SSL built-in class 'Email' uses curly braces for instantiation: 'Email{}' not 'Email()'
8:14-8:22 error class_instantiation_curly: SSL built-in class 'SSLRegex' uses curly braces for instantiation: 'SSLRegex{}' not 'SSLRegex()'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
